#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186107164 :tutorial/content "To find the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence given two arbitrary terms, we must usually apply the following:\n\n- The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by\n$a_n = a_1 + (n-1)d$\nwhere $a_n$ is the $n$th term, $a_1$ is the first term, and $d$ is the common difference.\n- We can find the common difference $d$ of an arithmetic sequence given two arbitrary terms using\n$d = \\frac{a_m-a_k}{m-k}$\nwhere $a_m$ is the $m$th term, and $a_k$ is the $k$th term.\n\nLet's see some examples." :tutorial/id #uuid "d021f3a1-b263-5fc0-a08d-cdec57045fb1" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8084 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
